---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="Why Alan Estate exists, who is building it, and what we believe about the weeks after a death.">
  <section class="container-x py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">About</p>
        <h1>Built by an executor, for the next one.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="prose text-ink-2">
        <p>Alan Estate started the way most of these things do: with a phone call, a filing cabinet, and eighteen months of finding out what we didn't know.</p>
        <p>One of us administered his father's estate. There was a self-managed super fund with individual trustees, invested directly across many managers. The binding nomination had lapsed four years earlier and nobody — not the family, not the accountant — knew. There was a reverse mortgage on the farm with terms no one had seen. Every fund, bank and agency needed its own certified paperwork, in its own format, and several of them still hadn't sent final statements a year later.</p>
        <p>What struck us afterwards wasn't that it was hard. It was that it was hard in a completely predictable way. The same forty tasks, in roughly the same order, with the same traps — and no one hands you the list.</p>
        <p>So we are writing the list first, and giving it away. Then we're building the tools around it: a personalised plan and drafted letters for executors, and a simple record for the living so their own family never has to search.</p>
        <h2>What we believe</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sequence is the product.</strong> Knowing that Centrelink is a two-week matter and probate is a two-month one changes everything about how a family copes.</li>
          <li><strong>Superannuation is where Australian estates go wrong.</strong> For most people over sixty it is the largest asset, it sits outside the will, and the rules for self-managed funds are unforgiving on timing.</li>
          <li><strong>Be honest about what we are.</strong> This is general information, carefully sourced, not legal advice. When something needs a lawyer or an SMSF specialist, we will say so plainly.</li>
          <li><strong>Grieving people are not a funnel.</strong> The guide has no paywall and no sign-up. If you want to hear from us, tell us. Otherwise, take what's useful and go.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Where we are</h2>
        <p>Early. The guide on this site is live and free. The products are in development, starting in Victoria. If you work with families or SMSF clients and see the same gap, we would genuinely like to talk: <a href="/professionals/">the founding partner pilot</a>. If you have lived this yourself and want to tell us what would have helped, <a href="/families/#waitlist">join the family waitlist</a> and use the note field — we read every one.</p>
        <p>Or just <a href="/contact/">write to us</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
